	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[WARNING:  pg_stop_backup still waiting for archive to complete]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=8006#p8006"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,</p><p>Je ne comprends pas, j&#039;ai de temps à autres le pg_stop_backup qui me fait des misères sur un pg 8.4 </p><p>Soit un bout de script tout bête :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>echo &quot;**************************************************&quot;
echo &quot;*            creation du backup                  *&quot;
echo &quot;**************************************************&quot;

$PSQLCMD &quot;CHECKPOINT;&quot;

$PSQLCMD &quot;SELECT pg_start_backup(&#039;scenario test $LABEL&#039;,true);&quot;

rm $HOME/data-db.tgz
tar zcvf $HOME/data-db.tgz $DATASQL


$PSQLCMD &quot;select pg_stop_backup();&quot;</code></pre></div><p>Et ça plante :<br />WARNING:&#160; pg_stop_backup still waiting for archive to complete (60 seconds elapsed)<br />WARNING:&#160; pg_stop_backup still waiting for archive to complete (120 seconds elapsed)<br />WARNING:&#160; pg_stop_backup still waiting for archive to complete (240 seconds elapsed)<br />WARNING:&#160; pg_stop_backup still waiting for archive to complete (480 seconds elapsed)</p><br /><br /><p>Pourtant, dans le .conf j&#039;ai bien archive_timeout = 300s<br />Donc je ne vois pas ce qui peut le bloquer...</p><p>J&#039;ai aussi essayé avec pg_start_backup(&#039;scenario test $LABEL&#039;) sans le &quot;true&quot; ça me fait pareil.</p><p>Il attend quoi le pg_stop_backup() exactement ?</p>]]></content>
